# Always on

- Never commit secrets, tokens, `.env`, or credentials. Use Vercel/dashboard env vars.
- Keep PRs small and scoped to the issue acceptance criteria.
- Follow issue acceptance criteria exactly; do not expand scope.
- Max 2 retries on failure. If still blocked, stop and ask for human help (`agent:needs-human`).
- Prefer existing scripts (`pnpm check`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm lint`) over new tooling.
- Docs-only agent issues (changes under `docs/` only): always run `pnpm check`; skip `pnpm build` unless acceptance criteria explicitly require it.
- Use `pnpm` (see `packageManager` in `package.json`). Content collection date field is `publishedDate` (not `pubDate`).
- Production host is Vercel (`tur-site`); deploy via `git push origin main` — do not switch hosts.
- When opening an agent Execute PR: mark **Ready for review** (not draft), **assign** `emilingemarkarlsson`, and **request review** from them when the author is cursor-bot — otherwise the PR never lands in https://github.com/pulls/assigned.
- Never merge your own agent PR; Emil approves. After Emil merges, they unassign themselves (GitHub does not clear assignees).
- **Meta-queue issues** (tracking issues without their own acceptance criteria): when all child issues are `agent:done`, close the meta-issue — remove `agent:ready`; do not leave it queued after the chain completes. If no `agent:draft` issues remain and open PRs await human merge, add a one-line queue-status note in `docs/agent-setup/GO_LIVE.md` instead of opening an empty code PR.
